# What gets uploaded when the browser client is deployed — see pwa/deploy.sh.
#
# The Vercel project's Root Directory is `pwa`, but the CLI uploads from *here*,
# because the client does not build from `pwa/` alone: `pwa/src/*` imports the
# sealed channel, the relay wire format, the pairing-link format and the brand
# from `src/shared/`, deliberately, so that there is one implementation of each
# rather than a browser copy that agrees with itself and drifts from the rest of
# the product.
#
# Without this file that upload is the whole working tree — 2.7 GB of it, nearly
# all `ios/`, `android/`, `release/` and `node_modules`. So this is an allowlist
# written the only way .gitignore syntax permits one: ignore everything at the
# top level, name back the two directories the build reads, then ignore
# everything inside `src/` except `shared/`. A negation cannot resurrect a file
# whose parent directory is ignored, which is why `/src` has to be un-ignored
# before `/src/*` is ignored again.
/*
!/pwa
!/src
/src/*
!/src/shared

# The repository's own `package.json`, which `pwa/vite.config.ts` reads for the
# version it stamps into the page. It is one file and it is not source, so it is
# easy to leave out of an allowlist written around directories — and leaving it
# out does not degrade the build, it **stops** it: the config throws `ENOENT`
# before vite starts, so every deploy since that read was added has failed and
# the live client has been serving whatever was there before. Found 2026-08-19,
# when the deployed app turned out to be older than the source.
!/package.json

# `pwa/src/protocol-client.ts` imports the wire protocol's own definition rather
# than restating it, which is the same argument `src/shared/` exists for and one
# the file makes at length. It has not moved into `shared/` yet, so the one file
# is named here.
!/src/main
/src/main/*
!/src/main/remote
/src/main/remote/*
!/src/main/remote/protocol.ts

# The two faces `pwa/src/styles.css` declares are the desktop's, by path —
# `../../src/renderer/assets/fonts/*.woff2` — so the client does not ship a
# second copy of a font the product already has. Vite resolves those at build
# time and fingerprints them into `dist/assets`; left out of the upload, the
# build does not fail, it *warns* and emits the URLs unchanged, which is a live
# page whose type falls back to whatever the phone happens to have. So the two
# files come too, and nothing else from the renderer does.
!/src/renderer
/src/renderer/*
!/src/renderer/assets
/src/renderer/assets/*
!/src/renderer/assets/fonts

# Built and installed by Vercel from pwa/package-lock.json. Uploading either
# would ship this Mac's copy — the wrong architecture for the build container in
# the first case, and in the second a `dist/` that predates the sources beside
# it, which is exactly the "folder somebody uploaded by hand" this deployment is
# not allowed to be.
/pwa/node_modules
/pwa/dist
